====================================================================================================
PART 1. DO LISTING EFFECTS DIFFER ACROSS COUNTRIES? MATCHED HORIZONS (service level)
====================================================================================================

--- one-year changes: year of listing (11 countries) vs one year before (11 countries) ---
  standard deviation: 0.70 vs 0.47; variance ratio 2.24
  F test (one-sided) p = 0.110 | Levene p = 0.146 | Brown-Forsythe p = 0.138

--- two-year changes: one year after (11 countries) vs two years before (10 countries) ---
  standard deviation: 1.03 vs 0.96; variance ratio 1.13
  F test (one-sided) p = 0.429 | Levene p = 0.965 | Brown-Forsythe p = 0.912

  Reading: differences across countries are supported only if the spread after listing is clearly
  larger than the spread before it over the SAME length of change, in all three tests.

