PART 5. BREAK-EVEN: HOW LARGE MUST UNRECORDED CHARGES BE? (2024 corridor-payout pairs)
====================================================================================================
Pairs: 236 (bank-account payouts: 81). As quoted: 34.3% of all pairs and 33.3% of bank-account pairs cost 5% or less.
  Charges added to EVERY pair halve the share of all pairs at or below 5% once they reach 1.4 points.
  Charges added to bank-account pairs halve their share once they reach 1.6 points, and leave none at or below 5% from 2.9 points.
  For comparison, the FSB ranges (recipient fees 0.1-1.8%, intermediary charges 0.1-3.4%) sum to 0.2 to 5.2 points.
